 addPanel('billing','Payment methods','<div class="card"><h2>Payment methods</h2><p>Card management will open the payment provider’s secure billing page after checkout is configured.</p><button disabled data-locked>Manage cards · not connected</button><p class="small">No full card numbers or security codes are collected or stored by this website.</p></div>');
 addPanel('guide','How It Works',`<div class="card"><h2>Collections &amp; the Recognition Wheel</h2><ol><li><h3>Choose a callsign group</h3><p>On the <strong>Current Collection</strong> page, choose an available callsign group from the dropdown. Each group has its own numbers and collection details.</p></li><li><h3>Select your number or numbers</h3><p>Choose one or more available numbers and complete checkout. Paid selections are recorded after payment is verified. FREE selections are recorded after you complete the claim.</p></li><li><h3>Follow the group</h3><p>When all numbers in a group have been purchased or assigned, the group is full. GAC will close the group and schedule a recognition time. Check the Current Collection page for group status.</p></li><li><h3>Watch the recognition wheel</h3><p>Select <strong>Recognition Wheel</strong> in the top navigation to view the group, countdown, and live spin when it begins.</p></li></ol><h3>Multiple Spins &amp; Recognition</h3><p>A callsign group can have multiple spins, and multiple members may be selected for recognition from the same group. The GAC Members Facebook page lists the order of the spins and how each selected member will be recognized. Check the latest post for the recognition details for each spin.</p><p><a href="https://www.facebook.com/share/1A1sJuvvVU/">View the GAC Members Facebook page</a></p><h3>What is a Mini?</h3><p>A Mini is a smaller, lower-priced group with its own spin. The selected entry advances to the associated main group’s recognition spin.</p><h3>GAC Callsign Recognition Rules</h3><ol><li><h4>State &amp; Local Laws</h4><p>Participants are responsible for knowing and complying with all applicable federal, state, and local firearm laws and restrictions.</p></li><li><h4>FFL Transfers</h4><p>Any firearm recognition item will be shipped only to a licensed FFL for transfer to the selected recipient. No substitutions or transfers to another individual.</p></li><li><h4>Age Requirement</h4><p>Participants must be 21 years of age or older.</p></li><li><h4>Background Check &amp; Eligibility</h4><p>Recipients must meet all legal requirements to receive their firearm. If denied or otherwise ineligible to complete the transfer, the firearm recognition item will be forfeited. Only the original entry cost will be refunded.</p></li></ol></div>`);
